4.2 Neuron Models

4.2.1 Leaky Integrate-and-Fire (LIF)

Mathematical Model:

```
τ_m * dV/dt = -(V - V_rest) + R_m * I_syn(t)

If V(t) ≥ V_thresh:
    Generate spike at time t
    V(t+) = V_reset
    Enter refractory period for τ_ref
```

Hardware Implementation:

```verilog
module lif_neuron #(
    parameter WIDTH = 8,
    parameter TAU_M = 20,  // 20 ms time constant
    parameter V_THRESH = 200,
    parameter V_RESET = 0,
    parameter TAU_REF = 2   // 2 ms refractory
)(
    input wire clk,
    input wire reset,
    input wire [WIDTH-1:0] I_syn,
    output reg spike
);
    
    reg [WIDTH-1:0] V;  // Membrane potential
    reg [7:0] ref_counter;
    
    always @(posedge clk) begin
        if (reset) begin
            V <= V_RESET;
            spike <= 0;
            ref_counter <= 0;
        end else begin
            if (ref_counter > 0) begin
                // In refractory period
                ref_counter <= ref_counter - 1;
                V <= V_RESET;
                spike <= 0;
            end else begin
                // Update membrane potential
                V <= V + ((I_syn - V) / TAU_M);
                
                // Check for spike
                if (V >= V_THRESH) begin
                    spike <= 1;
                    V <= V_RESET;
                    ref_counter <= TAU_REF;
                end else begin
                    spike <= 0;
                end
            end
        end
    end
endmodule
```

